<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Title 3"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title" idx="4294967295"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="340961" y="342685"/><a:ext cx="11282796" cy="423125"/></a:xfrm><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="A100FF"/></a:solidFill></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr vert="horz" lIns="91440" tIns="45720" rIns="91440" bIns="45720" rtlCol="0" anchor="ctr"><a:normAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="2000" b="1" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Graphik" panose="020B0503030202060203" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Proposed solution (200 words)</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="20" name="Body TextBox"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="361458" y="1099999"/><a:ext cx="11692890" cy="5415315"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0"><a:normAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>ShadowLine is a digital twin of the assembly line that runs four hours ahead of it.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>We deliberately do not build a photorealistic 3D factory. The twin is a lightweight discrete-event model of what actually determines output: station cycle times, station states (active, blocked, starved), buffer levels, and the genealogy of each part. Weld physics, robot kinematics and CAD geometry are skipped.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>Four layers. The signal layer reads what plants already emit: PLC station states, buffer counts, take deviation, torque and vision logs. No new hardware, so no retrofit capex. The twin core mirrors the live line. Three prediction heads run on top: bottleneck forecasting, using the Active Period Method (which identifies bottlenecks from uninterrupted active time alone) with Monte Carlo simulation of the next four hours, re-forked every 60 seconds; defect propagation, a learned station to station lag graph that traces an end of line failure back to its causing station; and virtual sensors, which infer state at manual or unsensored stations from neighbouring buffer levels and takt deviation. The action layer issues ranked alerts carrying cause, confidence and time to impact.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>The output is not a dashboard. It is one line to a supervisor: “Station 14, 73% likely to bottleneck by 14:20.”</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{BB962C8B-B14F-4D97-AF65-F5344CB8AC3E}"><p14:creationId xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" val="2205980423"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>